      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The coexistence of a coronary artery obstructive disease (CAOD) with aorto-iliac obstructive disease (AIOD) often represents a surgical problem. Because of left main coronary disease (LMCOD) the contemporary correction of AIOD should be performed with a simple non traumatic procedure. The case of a high risk patient in whom aortoiliac obstructive disease has been corrected with the implantation of a bifurcated vascular prosthesis from the ascending aorta to the bilateral common femoral arteries, and with a double aorto-coronary by-pass, is reported."},
